        "ipa": "ɪnˈveɪsɪv",
        "pos": "adj.",
        "meaningZh": "侵入的"
      }
    ],
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A student project has "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "revealed",
            "ref": "v-reveal"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " yet another power of AI: It can be good at locating where photos are taken."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The project is called Predicting Image Geolocations (or PIGEON). It’s the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of three Stanford students: Michal Skreta, Silas Alberti, and Lukas Haas. They designed it to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "identify",
            "ref": "v-identify"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " locations on "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Google Street View",
            "zh": "谷歌街景"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The team also showed the AI a few personal photos it had never seen before. To their surprise, the program was able to identify "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the photos were taken in most cases."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "PIGEON works well because it can "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " all the little things in photos. It can notice small differences in leaves, soil, and weather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The group says the technology can be "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in many ways. It could identify roads or power lines that need fixing. It may also help researchers do surveys of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "invasive",
            "ref": "v-invasive"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " plant species in a region."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Skreta believes "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people will find it useful as well. “You like this destination in Italy. Where in the world could you go if you want to see something similar?” he says."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", this new power is likely to be a double-edged sword. It could be used to reveal people’s private, personal information, says Jay Stanley, an expert at the American Civil Liberties Union."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Stanley worries that companies might soon use AI to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " where you’ve travelled. Governments might check your photos to see if you’ve visited certain countries. "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Stalking",
            "zh": "跟踪"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is also a possible threat, he says. People have long been able to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " GPS location information from photos they post online. That may not work anymore."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p9",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The Stanford students are well aware of the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Because of these worries, they haven’t given the public access to their program."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p10",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Stanley thinks AI for location identification will become even more powerful in the future. What will that mean? Well, be very "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " about what’s in the background in the photos you post online!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
